            "review_title": "Review at Cuisine de Vin",
            "review_text": "Thao D\nCape Town, South Africa335 contributions\n0\nLittle surprise package: Western food comes with the Vietnamese price.\nFeb 2017\nYes really, this Viet-owner restaurant has offered the Western food for just the Viet price. More specific, it's the Italian food, mostly spaghetti cooked with the French influence. \nThe resto itself locates at 123 Ly Tu Trong street, hence quite easy to find. Recently, they got 2nd resto opened up in Nguyen Chi Thanh str, but the one on Ly Ty Trong still my favorite one. The house could not be more simple, nice atmosphere and seemed like easy-going.\n\nThe spaghetti are so delicious, I did love the oven-bake spaghetti. So creamy and yet delightful!. The steak with black pepper sauce over was also nice, but 3 small slices of white sandwiches laying on the side seemed not bond together with the fries and steak. The cheese dipping sauce's the savor for the fries. Their brûlée is a must try as you were there. Nice touch to finish the meal. \nTheir chinaware's elegant, one of the plus points.\n\nThere's one point may need to improve, it's is the service. Don't get me wrong, the staffs were all welcoming and friendly, but lack of pro. skill and attentive. They served our first course without the cuttery, no napkin on the table and pouring bottled water without asking ice or no ice. Oh yeh, it's not like any fine dining restaurant, and they got really busy over the dinner time, so you apparently just could not ask for the better service. Well, you kinda just have to help yourself if you are sitting at table far away from the kitchen/serve station.\n\nOverall, the quality of food and the very reasonable price, style and spirit that being carried by the own couple had made it all. And it's still my favorite place to go for Western food in Danang. \nTip: try the oven-bake spaghetti and you do need the table reservation.\nRead more\nWritten February 19, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-04",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
